{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REACHABILITY BUG found on story B by live experiment, and fixed. Three live --source local runs showed the criterion FIRING correctly (validity 1.0, twice per run, naming both omitted files including the monkeypatch.setattr string site at test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:90) - but the coach never selected OUR move; it picked built-ins. Root cause, and it is a design problem not a config typo: the SAME incomplete-inventory evidence also fires rebar's BUILT-IN G1G2/G6/E4 criteria, which are agent-tier and BLOCKING, while this project criterion must stay ADVISORY per its own AC. Pass-4's coachable union is 'blocking findings first, then surviving advisory' (plan_review_coach_inputs_output), so a move keyed only on the advisory project id competes last and in practice is never offered - a dead move by construction, which is precisely the failure mode the plan-review gate warned about for the CODE-review routing. Fix (pure overlay config): applies_when widened to [project.symbol-reference-completeness, G1G2, G6] so the Serena coaching is reachable from the built-in inventory findings too, while still NOT firing for empty triggers, project.portability, or security/tests. This also meant my own held-out test encoded the WRONG contract ('fires only for this criterion'); corrected under revert-first discipline - narrowed the config back, confirmed the two new assertions RED for the right reason, re-applied, then GREEN. 20/21 tests pass; the only remaining failure is the committed evidence artifact. Also verified there is NO closed enum on the coach's move_id, so a project move is structurally pickable - the problem was trigger keying, not schema."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785379925419856001,"uuid":"77975626-58de-4aa6-8e22-2ada8deda21e"}